WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome to the show.
-Thanks, man.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:02.569 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Nice to be here.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:03.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is very fun
to see you in a comedy.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like we know
you from more serious roles.

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.607 size:84% position:42%
Are you enjoying doing
something that's funny?

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is the best job
in the world.

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:10.143 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Although, I was funny on

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Practice" and
"American Horror Story."

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah? Oh, really?
-Right?

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:13.913 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, okay.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:17.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
I maybe slightly missed
the jokes, yeah.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you hosted
"SNL" in 1999.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.588 size:84% position:42%
You met Will Ferrell
and you met Adam McKay,

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
the head writer
at "SNL" at the time.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they brought this
idea to you.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.026 line:92%
Was it pretty much a no-brainer

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you hear from
guys like this,

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they want you
to star in their comedy?

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.030 line:92%
-Oh, my God. Are you kidding me?

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you seen the show?
Captain Dave?

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:34.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's perfect.
-The greatest role ever.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I mean, I just -- I love it.

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:39.639
-And you get to have a mustache.
That's your mustache.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.707 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Most importantly, yes.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.977
-Did you base your mustache
on any historic mustaches?

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:47.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, when I
started to read the script,

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
the mustache started to
spontaneously grow by itself.

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
-Which was weird.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:54.154 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:56.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
The mustache
jumped off the page.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It did.
-Yeah.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:58.091 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It did.

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:59.426
But, I mean, you have to look at
the history of mustaches.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:03.596
Who has the best mustache ever?
-I mean, Selleck.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Selleck. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:05.432 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-You got to start there.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:07.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you
move down to Burt Reynolds.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
No, that's a pretty good one.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not very far down.
He's right beneath him, yeah.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then you've got to
go to Captain Dave.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Oh, you're third all time?

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:15.508 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I'm third all time.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:18.812
-I'm very jealous, because I was
hoping it was a fake mustache,

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:21.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I can tell that
you grew your own.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.082 line:92%
I cannot grow my own mustache,

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's very
heartbreaking for me,

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:26.753
because my father has a good --
a thick, bushy mustache.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:27.187 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Nice.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, yet,
I did not get that DNA.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:29.489 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But do you mind?

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can I put a mustache on
for the rest of the interview?

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would love that.
-Great. Okay.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.360 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
Couple of guys with mustaches.
-Wow.

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:39.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, totally.
-Wait a second.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's go side by side.
-Right there.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:44.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, no. We'll go over here.
We'll go to 3.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a good mustache.
-I love it.

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:49.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You --
-Tell me.

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:52.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did stand-up.
You used to try stand-up.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
You did stand-up
at the Comedy Cellar,

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:56.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
maybe the most famous
comedy place --

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:57.517 line:92%
stand-up place in New York.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.619
-But before we get into that,
I want to give you something.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:00.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got you something.
-Oh.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:04.924 size:84% position:42%
This is very exciting.
-No, that's my license.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.493 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Yeah, I got you this.

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:12.532
-This is...Heidi Klum Intimates?
-Yeah.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:13.366 line:92%
-Why did you get me this?

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:17.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't talk about it.
-Okay.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.372
I like that you leave the house,
and you're like,

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:23.409 size:78% position:39%
"I need two things --
my driver's license

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.278 line:92%
and some Heidi Klum Intimates."

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:26.446 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
These are...

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:30.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
These go over the nipple.
-That's right.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:33.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Clears throat ]
-All right.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I put on a mustache.
-Yeah, you might as well.

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:41.694
-So, anyways, you go at the
Cellar, and it didn't go great?

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, yeah, I did
Catch A Rising Star,

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:44.764 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The Bitter End,

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:47.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, you know, I was
feelin' myself a little bit.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did the Comedy Cellar.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'm up there,
and it's not going well.

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:55.074
-Mm-hmm. How'd you know?
-Well, no one's laughing.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.342 line:92%
-Yeah, that's how you know.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:59.546
-So, when no one laughs --
and it was really crickets --

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:03.049 size:84% position:42%
they pulled me offstage
and they threw me out.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.517 size:75% position:38%
They threw me out of
the Comedy Cellar.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.920
-Wow. And that's a pretty --
And, you know, people say,

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How do you know
it's not going well?"

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:11.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's really how you know.
-Yeah.

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
Go ahead.
-Okay, great. Thank you.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.461
Wow. I don't quite know what --
All right.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:18.298
-You want me to help you?
-No, I think I got it.

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:21.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think this has been
intimate enough.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:22.435 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh!

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
-Nice.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:29.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's -- It's like...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:33.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
I look like
a sheriff in a musical.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:36.549 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.318 size:84% position:42%
-This is one of my --
I was at "SNL" in 2012,

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:40.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we did a sketch called --
It was a game show called

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Dylan McDermott
or Dermot Mulroney?"

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:43.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:47.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have --
And now Dermot Mulroney plays

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:50.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
a rival captain on the show,
which is fantastic.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:51.164 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But that was true.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:52.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys got mistaken
for each other for years.

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:56.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, the name has been a
nightmare for 30 years.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
-30 years.
-30 years.

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because you guys
really came on the scene

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.473 line:92%
at almost the exact same time.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.341 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, that's right.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:04.310 size:78% position:39%
And it's been painful
for many, many years.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:04.978 size:75% position:38% line:92%
As a matter of fact,

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
we both were at
William Morris at the time.

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:09.382
Sue Mengers was the biggest
agent in the world at the time.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:11.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
She came up to me
in the hallway and she said --

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:13.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
Walked right up to me
and she said,

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:17.724 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"There can only be one."

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:19.292 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And I said, "One what?"

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.927 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"There can only be one."

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:23.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, she -- "You have to
change your name."

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:25.131 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I was like, "Oh, no!"

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:30.336
So, I came up with the
fantastic name of Mick Dermott.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:35.074 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:35.842 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I am glad, in the end,

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:38.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you stood your ground
on your God-given name.

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:43.082
Well, it's very nice that
this 30-year name mix-up

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:45.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
has now collided with
you guys working together.

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:47.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
He finally came on the show.

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:47.820 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He was wonderful.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:52.892
And, you know, we wanted to
finally add more confusion,

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:53.459 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
which we did.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:54.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:56.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congrats on the show.
Such a pleasure.

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.197 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

